    id: "goplus-375hp-cheap-incline",
    name: "Goplus 3.75HP Folding Treadmill with Incline",
    brand: "Goplus",
    category: "Folding treadmill with 15% automatic incline",
    badge: "Best Overall",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B09D814HYX?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41CduzRJ71L._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $430 (Amazon, 9 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":430,"high":430},
    specs: "1–15% automatic incline · 52 x 17 in. belt · 3.75 HP · 265 lb capacity · 12 preset + 3 custom programs · soft-drop folding · about 140 lb",
    pros: [
      "The longest belt here, 52 inches, for room to stride on a hill",
      "Automatic incline from 1 to 15%",
      "Soft-drop folding and four transport wheels",
      "Handrail heart-rate sensors, Bluetooth speakers and app control",
    ],
    cons: [
      "265 lb capacity, the lowest of the powered machines here",
      "Top speed not given in the bullet points we read",
      "No warranty term in the bullets; check with the seller",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The best balance of belt length and powered incline under $500, for walkers comfortably under 265 lb.",
    description: "Goplus’s 3.75 HP folding treadmill earns the top spot because it pairs a steep powered incline with a belt long enough to use it. The listing gives an automatic incline from 1 to 15%, 12 preset programs and three user-defined programs with time, distance and calorie countdowns, and a five-layer, anti-slip belt of 52 by 17 inches, the longest on this page. It quotes a 3.75 HP motor and a 265 lb maximum load. A five-inch LCD shows time, speed, distance, calories, heart rate and program; there are four Bluetooth speakers, app control, two heart-rate handrails and a safety key. It folds vertically with a soft-drop system and rolls on four wheels; Amazon gives the weight as 140 lb. It was $429.99 on 9 November 2026. The weak points are capacity, at 265 lb, and the listing’s silence on top speed and warranty. If you are well under the limit and mainly walk, it gives the most usable incline for the money.",
  },
  {
    id: "merach-t16-cheap-incline",
    name: "MERACH T16 Incline Treadmill",
    brand: "MERACH",
    category: "Compact folding treadmill with 15% powered incline",
    badge: "Best for Walkers",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0HJ2FC1JW?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/4198sRIBAHL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $400 (Amazon, 9 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":400,"high":400},
    specs: "0–15% auto incline, 15 levels · 43.5 x 16.5 in. belt · 0.6–7.5 mph · 3.0 HP brushless · 300 lb capacity · about 92 lb",
    pros: [
      "Powered incline to 15% with controls on the console and handrails",
      "300 lb rating, higher than the Goplus",
      "Arrives about 98% pre-assembled, per the listing",
      "Light for a treadmill, at about 92 lb",
    ],
    cons: [
      "A 43.5-inch belt is short for a brisk stride on a steep incline",
      "7.5 mph top speed: walking and easy jogging only",
      "No warranty term in the bullet points we read",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For walkers of average height who want handrails, a 300 lb rating and powered incline for about $400.",
    description: "Merach’s T16 is a compact folding treadmill built around incline walking. The listing gives 15 powered incline levels up to 15%, a 3.0 HP brushless motor, speeds of 0.6 to 7.5 mph and a 300 lb capacity, with a 43.5 by 16.5-inch five-layer belt, six shock-absorbing pads and handrails. Controls sit on both the console and the handrails, so you can raise the incline without reaching forward, and there are 15 preset programs and app syncing. Merach says it arrives 98% pre-assembled. Amazon gives its weight as 92 lb, light enough for most people to fold and roll. It was $399.98 on 9 November 2026. Against the Goplus, it trades eight and a half inches of belt for a higher weight rating, handrail controls and a lighter frame. The shorter belt is the reason it is second: on a steep incline you drift back, and taller walkers may find 43.5 inches tight. For shorter walkers and anyone nearer 300 lb, it may be the better buy. Our Merach guide covers the rest of the range.",
  },
  {
    id: "therun-12-cheap-incline",
    name: "THERUN Incline Treadmill, 0-12% Auto Incline",
    brand: "THERUN",
    category: "Cheapest folding treadmill with powered incline",
    badge: "Best Value",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0DJ8F6DZP?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41TP5tk6XaL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $340 (Amazon, 9 Nov 2026)",
    priceBounds: {"low":340,"high":340},
    specs: "0–12% auto incline, 12 levels · 43.3 x 16.5 in. belt · 0.5–9 mph · 3.0 HP · 300 lb capacity · folding · about 110 lb",
    pros: [
      "Powered incline to 12% for about $340",
      "300 lb rating",
      "A 9 mph top speed, faster than the Merach",
      "Four internal shock absorbers plus two cushioning layers",
    ],
    cons: [
      "A 43.3-inch belt, among the shortest here",
      "Listing calls it a walking pad in places, a hint at its real use",
      "No warranty term in the bullet points we read",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The cheapest way on this list to get a powered incline, for walkers who do not need a long belt.",
    description: "THERUN’s 12% auto-incline treadmill is the cheapest machine here with a motorised incline. The listing gives 12 levels of automatic incline from 0 to 12%, a 3.0 HP motor, speeds of 0.5 to 9 mph and a 300 lb user rating, on a 43.3 by 16.5-inch belt with what THERUN calls 2+4 shock absorption: four internal absorbers and two extra layers of non-slip cushioning. It folds for storage and the listing describes assembly as straightforward. Amazon gives the weight as 110 lb. It was $339.99 on 9 November 2026. A 12% ceiling is all the incline most walkers will use, and 9 mph gives a little jogging headroom, but the belt is the limitation: at 43.3 inches it is fine for walking at an average stride and short for jogging. The listing refers to it as a walking pad at points, which is a fair way to think of it. The bullet points give no warranty term, so ask the seller before you buy.",
  },
  {
    id: "therun-15-47-cheap-incline",
    name: "THERUN Incline Treadmill, 0-15% Auto Incline, 47.2 in. Belt",
    brand: "THERUN",
    category: "Folding treadmill with 15% incline and a longer belt",
    badge: "Worth Stretching For",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BTSWT8T2?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41WrqXOZEWL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
