        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>What is the cheapest treadmill with incline?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The cheapest on this page, on 9 November 2026, was the SereneLife Folding Treadmill at about $240, with four manual incline levels. The cheapest with powered incline was the THERUN 0-12% Auto Incline treadmill at about $340.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is auto incline worth it on a cheap treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For most people, yes. On this page the gap between the cheapest manual and powered models is about $100, and the powered ones reach 12 to 15% against about 6% for manual. You can change a powered incline mid-walk, so you are more likely to use it.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you get a 15% incline treadmill under $500?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Yes. On 9 November 2026 the Goplus 3.75HP Folding Treadmill (about $430) and the Merach T16 (about $400) both listed powered incline to 15%. A THERUN with 15% incline and a longer belt was about $530.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Are cheap incline treadmills good for running?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not really. Most have belts of 39 to 52 inches and top speeds of 6 to 9 mph where stated. They suit incline walking and light jogging. For regular running, spend more on a longer belt and a stronger motor.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What weight capacity should a cheap incline treadmill have?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              At least 25% above your body weight. Incline walking loads the motor more at a given speed, and budget ratings are best treated as ceilings. The machines here are rated 265 to 300 lb.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Do cheap incline treadmills fold?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              All six on this page fold upright for storage, most with a soft-drop or hydraulic mechanism. Folded size varies widely, from about 22 by 24 inches of floor for the SereneLife to about 49 by 26 inches for the Merach T12.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

